  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, the amount received by the sons&nbsp;be Rs. <math><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math> Rs. <math><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and Rs <math><mi>z</mi></math> respectively,&nbsp;then</p><p><math><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>101</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>101</mn></math> .<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></math><br />So, the required number of ways is the coefficient of&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>101</mn></mrow></msup></math> in <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>51</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />or&nbsp;coefficient of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>101</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;in the expansion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>50</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>or coefficient of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>101</mn></msup></math> in the expansion of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>51</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />or coefficient of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>101</mn></msup></math> in the expansion of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>51</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />or coefficient of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>101</mn></msup></math> in the expansion of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>51</mn></msup><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>×</mo><mn>103</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>101</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>52</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>50</mn></msub><msup><mo>=</mo><mn>103</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>52</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>",
